---
import C from "../components/C.astro";
import CodeCard from "../components/CodeCard.astro";
import P from "../components/P.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import { REPO } from "../lib/links";

const PROMPTS = [
  "Add a playthru demo of the issue composer to the hero.",
  "Put a self-playing demo of this page in the landing page, no npm.",
  "My playthru demo starts the second loop in the wrong state. Fix it.",
].join("\n");
---

<Section id="install" title="Install">
  <P>
    The quickest way is to let your coding agent do it. Add the{" "}
    <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/skills/playthru/SKILL.md`} class="article-link">agent skill</a> to your project.
  </P>
  <CodeCard title="Agent skill" lang="sh" code="npx skills add diip3sh/playthrou" />
  <P>
    Then ask in plain words. The skill tells the agent how playthru works, so it can install it (or load it from a CDN on a
    plain HTML page), build the stage, write the script and the reset, and mirror your hover styles.
  </P>
  <CodeCard title="Prompts" lang="text" code={PROMPTS} />
  <P>To set it up by hand, add the package. It has no dependencies and no stylesheet to import.</P>
  <CodeCard title="Terminal" lang="sh" code="npm i playthru" />
  <P>Wrap the UI you want to show in a stage, then write the script.</P>
  <CodeCard
    title="hero.html"
    lang="html"
    code={`<div id="hero" class="h-[520px]">\n  <div><!-- your real app UI --></div>\n</div>`}
  />
  <CodeCard
    title="hero.ts"
    lang="ts"
    code={`import { playthru } from "playthru";\n\nplaythru("#hero")\n  .click("#new-issue")\n  .zoom("#composer")\n  .type("#title", "Fix onboarding flicker on Safari")\n  .click("#create")\n  .zoomOut()\n  .zoom(".issue:first-child")\n  .reset(() => app.reset());`}
  />
  <P>
    It starts the first time the stage scrolls into view and loops forever. In React, import <C>Playthru</C> from{" "}
    <C>playthru/react</C> and pass the same chain as a function.
  </P>
  <CodeCard
    title="Hero.jsx"
    lang="jsx"
    code={`<Playthru\n  className="h-[520px]"\n  script={(d) => d.type("#todo", "Record the launch video").click("#add")}\n>\n  <TodoApp />\n</Playthru>`}
  />
</Section>
